# Root .dockerignore - needed because chat-ui/Dockerfile builds from the
# repo root (it needs to COPY docs/ and README.md, which live outside its
# own directory - see that Dockerfile's own comment). Without this, every
# service's node_modules/.next/build output gets swept into that context
# too, which is both slow and can fail outright on stray files (e.g. broken
# symlinks Next.js's file tracing can leave in .next/).
**/node_modules
**/.next
**/dist
.git
